{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>The two sons of — I will kill.</b> He undertook with an oath to bring him to his father, for he said to him: <b>The two sons of me you will kill</b> (אֶת שְׁנֵי בָנַי תָּמִית) in the event that I do not bring him back to you, and it is like what Judah said to him (Genesis 43:9), <b>then I will have sinned against you all the days.</b> And he said <b>the two sons of me</b> (אֶת שְׁנֵי בָנַי) though they were four, to say: in place of the one of your sons there shall be a doubling in my sons. And behold, Jacob did not trust Reuben as he trusted Judah, because Judah had authority among his brothers, and furthermore because Reuben had already transgressed against his father and he would not trust him. And the general principle is that Judah's counsel was good, to leave the old man be until the bread of the household is exhausted (cf. Tanhuma, Mikeitz 8), for then he would listen, and that is what he said to him: <b>that we may live and not die, both we and our little ones.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:13.136028491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}